text Yet I'm still sitting here in the lukewarm water that is the Furukawa house.
text The worker I met then wasn't much older than I am now... and I recall that shocking me as well.
text @[Tomoya]
text (But I'm still here...)
text I feel irritated while I also start recalling all sorts of things.
text Including the fact that I'd be fairly compensated for that kind of struggle.
text With that kind of money, I could live on my own, without having to rely on the old man and Sanae-san.
text I squint my eyes to try to make out the worker's face.
text He's too far to see clearly, but I think that his physique is similar.
text It's fine if I'm wrong. Driven by my impatience, I run toward him.
